        "body": "there are 2 `CONTRIBUTING.md` files.\n* [`/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`](https://github.com/lysine-dev/okhttp/blob/5a4b597d11b719128dd8f87e3ef8657286734c64/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n* [`/CONTRIBUTING.md`](https://github.com/lysine-dev/okhttp/blob/5a4b597d11b719128dd8f87e3ef8657286734c64/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n\nThe .github one takes precedence in the root ([ref](https://docs.github.com/en/communities/setting-up-your-project-for-healthy-contributions/setting-guidelines-for-repository-contributors#:~:text=If%20a%20repository%20contains%20more%20than%20one%20CONTRIBUTING%20file%2C%20then%20the%20file%20shown%20in%20links%20is%20chosen%20from%20locations%20in%20the%20following%20order%3A%20the%20.github%20directory%2C%20then%20the%20repository%27s%20root%20directory%2C%20and%20finally%20the%20docs%20directory.)).  However it appears as though the intention is to use the one in the root.\n\nThe one in `.github/` should be removed and the one from the root should be moved to the `.github/` directory.\n\nyou can see the effective contributing guidelines in the main project page byt clicing in the \"Contributing\" tab, or following the contributing link in the project metadata -> https://github.com/lysine-dev/okhttp/?tab=contributing-ov-file\n\n<img width=\"725\" height=\"476\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/08afd2ad-f8a9-4d08-8b3d-51ab0083e27a\" />\n\n\n",
